    "answer": {
      "short": "In row order: $17^{\\circ}\\mathrm C$, $23^{\\circ}\\mathrm C$, $31^{\\circ}\\mathrm C$, $10^{\\circ}\\mathrm C$, $5^{\\circ}\\mathrm C$, $15^{\\circ}\\mathrm C$, $16^{\\circ}\\mathrm C$.",
      "worked": "Increase = maximum temperature − minimum temperature.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}6-(-11)&=6+11=17^{\\circ}\\mathrm C\\\\7-(-16)&=7+16=23^{\\circ}\\mathrm C\\\\-4-(-35)&=-4+35=31^{\\circ}\\mathrm C\\\\-15-(-25)&=-15+25=10^{\\circ}\\mathrm C\\\\-2-(-7)&=-2+7=5^{\\circ}\\mathrm C\\\\2-(-13)&=2+13=15^{\\circ}\\mathrm C\\\\5-(-11)&=5+11=16^{\\circ}\\mathrm C\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
